NAME
       mount - mount a filesystem, or list what is mounted

SYNOPSIS
       mount
       mount device path

DESCRIPTION
       With no arguments, lists every mounted filesystem. With a device
       and a path, mounts that device there. The filesystem type is
       detected from the superblock; ext2, ext4, FAT32, ISO 9660 and
       UDF are recognised.

EXAMPLES
       mount
       mount /dev/sda1 /mnt

SEE ALSO
       umount(1), lsblk(1), mkfs(1), mount9(1), df(1)
